{
  "schema": "wotex.coap.native-contract@1",
  "status": "executed",
  "runner_contract": "Inputs drive a real native IPC decoder/helper; expected values remain ExUnit-owned. Traces name test-controlled events, not helper answers. Native durable-state cases require the compiled helper and local store. An authenticated_response is protected by the runner's RFC 8613 peer for the helper request named by answers, whose kid and Partial IV form the AAD; an Observe option value is sent as the response Partial IV with an empty Inner Observe option. {request, field} substitutes the message_id or token that request carried on the wire, and {fresh_message_id} selects a Message ID the trace has not used. The helper's tokens are random, so a trace cannot fix a token value. A credit trace establishes the named subscription with request 17 and reads every frame. The acknowledged registration response is the first report of its first produce_complete_single_frame_reports step; each further report is a non-confirmable notification with the next Partial IV and a distinct payload; grant_report_credit sends credit with ack_seq 0; suspend_beam_owner means no further credit; validate_report_frames_through reads report frames through that report_seq. authenticated_notification sends one non-confirmable notification with the next Partial IV, protected for request 17. The native terminal envelope carries a finite library code; session_lost is a Runtime transport status, not a native code. sequence_boundary executes in the native store-send vector, where libcoap refuses a send at next sender sequence 2^40 before encryption and the durable store reports sequence_exhausted for a reservation past 2^40; a helper context cannot reach that sequence because each opens at zero and is consumed on exit. produce_report_payload expands its repeat_byte payload; the registration response carries the first one, and each payload is sent as protected 1,024-byte Block2 blocks with one ETag, the runner serving every follow-up block request.",
